Sure! Below is a minimal example of an “interactive card” that flips (rotates) when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** – no JavaScript needed.

---

### 1️⃣ Markup (HTML)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Obracająca się karta</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-face front">
            <h2>Tytuł karty</h2>
            <p>To jest przednia strona karty.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-face back">
            <h2>Inny tytuł</h2>
            <p>To jest tylną stronę karty.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

* `card-wrapper` – container that keeps the card centered and gives perspective.  
* `card` – element that will actually rotate.  
* Two child elements (`front` & `back`) represent the two sides of the card.

---

### 2️⃣ Styling (CSS)

Create a file called `style.css` (or put the styles inside a `<style>` tag).

```css
/* Basic reset */
*, *::before, *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

/* Center the wrapper vertically & horizontally */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;          /* width of the card */
    height: 200px;         /* height of the card */
    margin: 100px auto;    /* center on page */
    perspective: 800px;    /* give depth to 3D effect */
}

/* Card itself */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.8s ease-in-out;   /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;             /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* Hover triggers rotation */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* rotate around Y‑axis (horizontal flip) */
}

/* Common face styling */
.card-face {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide backside while rotating */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #fff;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
}

/* Front side */
.front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b);
}

/* Back side – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43cea2, #185a9d);
    transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* start flipped */
}
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| 1 | `.card-wrapper` sets a **perspective** so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| 2 | `.card` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so its children stay in 3D space. |
| 3 | Each face (`.card-face`) has `backface-visibility: hidden` – the side facing away from us disappears during rotation. |
| 4 | On hover, `.card` rotates 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| 5 | The back face was initially rotated 180°, so after the card’s rotation it becomes visible. |

---

### 🎨 Customization tips

| Property | What you can change |
|----------|---------------------|
| `width / height` of `.card-wrapper` | Size of the card |
| `perspective` | Depth of the 3D effect (larger → more subtle) |
| `transition` duration | Speed of the flip |
| `background` gradients | Colors or images for each side |
| `rotateY(180deg)` | Use `rotateX(180deg)` for vertical flip, or combine both for a 3‑D twist |

Feel free to copy the code into your project and tweak the colors, fonts, or dimensions to match your design!
